     </tr>
    </thead><tbody>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1046310">EVEX.LLIG.F2.0F.W0 79 /r</para>
      <para unique="1046311">VCVTSD2USI r32, xmm1/m64{er}</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046315">A</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046317">V/V</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046322">AVX512F</para>
      <para unique="1046326">OR AVX10.1<anchor id="+503795"/></para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046328">Convert one double precision floating-point value from xmm1/m64 to one unsigned doubleword integer r32.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1046290">EVEX.LLIG.F2.0F.W1 79 /r</para>
      <para unique="1046291">VCVTSD2USI r64, xmm1/m64{er}</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046295">A</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046300">V/N.E.<footnote><para unique="1046299" format="TableFootnote">EVEX.W1 in non-64 bit is ignored; the instruction behaves as if the W0 version is used.</para>
        </footnote></para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046305">AVX512F</para>
      <para unique="1046306">OR AVX10.1 <anchor id="+138238"/></para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1046308">Convert one double precision floating-point value from xmm1/m64 to one unsigned quadword integer zero-extended into r64.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
